# Code review format (Themis)

When reviewing PRs, structure findings exactly as:

## Summary
…

## Blocking issues
None.

## Suggestions
None.

## High priority issues
None.

## Risks
None.

## Nits
None.

If nothing blocking and no material risks/nits: a single line is allowed:

`LGTM - no blocking issues found.`

Rules:
- No secrets in git (`.env`, QBO tokens, SQL passwords, `.secrets/`)
- `gate:mr` must pass (`npm test` + `dotnet test`)
- Week-1 scope per `docs/planning/Week1-Demo-Plan.md` — do not expand to full WBS in one PR
- .NET 8 + EF Core + SQL Server + React; QuickBooks sandbox only (no production keys)
- Use `Related: #N` in PRs — never `Fixes #N` before Argus PASS
- OpenSpec for non-trivial product behavior
